# Keys of hot-text.list (every tier) that may name a function without a fixed boundary
# (LAYOUT-HOTKEY-INLINE-STABLE; `cargo xtask static`, xtask/src/hottext.rs `check_pinned`). Every other Rust key
# must name a #[inline(never)] function. <v0 key> TAB <tier> TAB <reason>; the tier is the key's tier in
# hot-text.list. A line whose key gained a fixed boundary, left the list or changed tier is an error. A ratchet
# (rulings #4997, #5024): lines may only be removed. These keys can still go dead when unrelated code moves
# LLVM's inlining budget; the build's dead-key check and `cargo xtask hottext-repair` remain their guard.
